Subject: [PATCH 39] predefine _LP64 alongside __LP64__ on LP64 targets

tcc predefines `__LP64__` on LP64 targets but not `_LP64`. Every other
compiler that targets the LP64 data model defines *both* spellings --
verified directly against gcc 15.2 on x86-64, which emits

    #define __LP64__ 1
    #define _LP64 1

The two names are not alternatives with a preferred spelling; they are a
pair, and portable code picks whichever one it happens to have been
written against. Code that tests only the one tcc omits does not fail to
compile -- it silently selects the compiler's 32-bit branch on a 64-bit
target, which is the worst available failure mode.

This was found the hard way. libressl's `include/openssl/bn.h` chooses its
bignum limb type with

    #if defined(_LP64) || defined(_WIN64)
    #define BN_ULONG        uint64_t
    #define BN_BITS2        64
    #else
    #define BN_ULONG        uint32_t
    #define BN_BITS2        32
    #endif

`__LP64__` is not consulted. So under tcc, amd64 libressl was building its
entire bignum layer on 32-bit limbs while the vendored s2n-bignum assembly
it calls reads and writes 64-bit ones. `make check` went 92/136, with 44
failures across every `bn_*` test and everything downstream of them --
rsa, dsa, ec, dh, cms, tls -- as `BN_add` dropped high words, `bn_div_words`
asserted, and glibc aborted on a corrupted heap. Defining `_LP64` and
changing nothing else takes that build to 136/136.

That is a data-model bug, not a libressl bug, and the same trap is set for
any other consumer that spells it `_LP64`. Fixing the single header check
downstream would have left it armed for the next one.

The define goes in the branch that already establishes LP64: the outer
conditional selects on `__SIZEOF_POINTER__ == 4` (ILP32), then
`__SIZEOF_LONG__ == 4` (LLP64, 64-bit Windows), and this `#else` is
reached only when pointer and long are both 64-bit. `_LP64` therefore
lands on exactly the targets it describes, and Win64 -- where neither gcc
nor MSVC defines it -- is untouched, as is the 32-bit branch.

Note that the 32-bit branch defines `__ILP32__` without `_ILP32`, the
mirror image of this gap. That is left alone here: nothing in this effort
builds a 32-bit target, so closing it would be an unmeasured change. It is
recorded in TODO.md instead.

Indentation is load-bearing in this file: only lines indented four or more
columns are emitted into the compiled-in predefs, and lines at column 1
are conditionals whose platform macros get substituted at conversion time.
The new line matches its neighbour exactly.

--- a/dep/tcc/include/tccdefs.h
+++ b/dep/tcc/include/tccdefs.h
@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@
     #define __SIZE_TYPE__ unsigned long
     #define __PTRDIFF_TYPE__ long
     #define __LP64__ 1
+    #define _LP64 1
 # if defined __linux__
     #define __INT64_TYPE__ long
 # else /* APPLE, BSD */
